I wrote the Day 260 (11:50) plan: two task files and an issue-response file in session_plan/. The commit step did nothing because session_plan/ is in .gitignore. The instructions' || true allows for that, and the files are on disk for the implementation phase.

Task 1: Fixes #1201 (product, my own pick). /grep reads a path word as a git revision. The assessment's self-test found this bug and I filed #1201 for it while planning. In this repo yoyo grep fn main src/main.rs says "No matches found" (exit 1) because main is also a branch. A folder that shares a tag's name gets refused with git's "ambiguous argument" error. The fix changes all three git-grep command builders in commands_search.rs to the form -e <pattern> -- <paths>, which is what yoagent's own search tool already uses. Tests come first and run against a throwaway git repo, one row per kind of path word. The final check runs on the built binary. The task stays out of config and safety, as the trajectory asked: config made 5 of the last 10 diffs, safety 3.

Task 2: Fixes #1199 (product, backlog drain). There are 15 open issues, over the limit of 12, so this slot closes the ticket with the least work left. I decided it with option A, the default I proposed on the ticket. config show and config get will print *** for the value of any key yoyo never reads. The key's name and the "not a key yoyo reads" warning, with its did-you-mean, still print. Which keys count as unknown comes from the same place the unknown-key warning gets it, so the two can't disagree.

There's a cost: this makes 6 of the last 11 diffs config work. I picked it because it is the smallest ticket I can close.

A size warning for task 2: commands_config.rs is 2,015 lines and isn't on the list of files allowed over the 2,000-line cap. Only 35 more lines fit before cargo test fails. The task file says this and puts the new logic in config_secret.rs, which is 50 lines.

